# M39.02 — BROWSER AND NODE.JS RUNTIME SEPARATION

## Objective

Permanently separate browser-safe application code from Node-specific process-management functionality.

## Known architectural problem

PHASE 38 REPORTED THAT:

`src/services/phase38Service.ts`

WAS IMPORTED THROUGH:

`src/services/automatedTestRunner.ts`

INTO BROWSER-FACING ADMINISTRATION VIEWS.

THE SERVICE CONTAINED NODE.JS DEPENDENCIES INCLUDING:

`child_process`

AND:

`path`

THIS CAUSED A VITE BROWSER RUNTIME FAILURE.

## Required architecture

ESTABLISH EXPLICIT RUNTIME BOUNDARIES.

### Browser-side responsibilities

BROWSER CODE MAY:

- DISPLAY TEST RESULTS.
- DISPLAY PERSISTENCE STATUS.
- DISPLAY READINESS REPORTS.
- REQUEST AUTHORIZED BACKEND VERIFICATION.
- PRESENT ERROR STATES.
- REFRESH VERIFICATION RESULTS.

BROWSER CODE MUST NOT:

- IMPORT NODE PROCESS EXECUTION MODULES.
- SPAWN OPERATING SYSTEM PROCESSES.
- EXECUTE SHELL COMMANDS.
- ACCESS SERVER FILESYSTEM PATHS DIRECTLY.
- EXECUTE DATABASE MIGRATIONS.
- RUN BACKEND VERIFICATION SCRIPTS.

### Server-side responsibilities

NODE.JS CODE MAY:

- EXECUTE APPROVED VERIFICATION TASKS.
- PERFORM CONTROLLED PROCESS-RESTART TESTS.
- READ AUTHORIZED DEVELOPMENT FILES.
- VALIDATE LOCAL PERSISTENCE.
- EXECUTE SERVER-SIDE TEST UTILITIES.

ALL SUCH OPERATIONS MUST REMAIN OUTSIDE THE BROWSER BUNDLE.

## Required implementation

INSPECT THE EXISTING SERVICE IMPORT GRAPH.

IDENTIFY SERVER-ONLY IMPORTS REACHABLE FROM CLIENT ENTRY POINTS.

SEPARATE SHARED DATA TYPES FROM SERVER IMPLEMENTATIONS.

USE SHARED TYPE DEFINITIONS OR BROWSER-SAFE INTERFACES WHERE APPROPRIATE.

MOVE NODE-SPECIFIC IMPLEMENTATIONS INTO EXPLICIT SERVER-ONLY MODULES.

USE BROWSER-SAFE API CLIENTS FOR AUTHORIZED VERIFICATION REQUESTS.

AVOID CIRCULAR IMPORTS.

PRESERVE EXISTING USER INTERFACES.

## Acceptance criteria

THE CLIENT APPLICATION NO LONGER IMPORTS NODE PROCESS-MANAGEMENT IMPLEMENTATIONS THROUGH ITS RUNTIME DEPENDENCY GRAPH.

